#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105906 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105562 :question/id #uuid "472216c8-da7d-58fb-9056-e71d5e33460d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3297" :question/problem "The area of $ABCD$ is $300\\, \\text{cm}^2.$  What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n![](images/c0/c06ffb123bdd24c3f83419767b6d1578223b8093089b79f91aae8f1fc6121305.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $\\triangle ACD.$ We get \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot DA\\cdot DC\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(25)(32)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =400\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =375.877... \\\\  & ≈376\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ and $\\triangle ACD$ gives the area of $\\triangle ABC.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & ={A}_{ACD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =376-300 \\\\  & =76\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561453 :question-generator/id #uuid "a3e0b970-d603-53ed-ae5e-4a3b84687b7a" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186105906.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79e7cd07-add5-5d10-80df-71a143f0f74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285917} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae3971d-6093-5438-8c3a-22800ae8c4ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285923} {:answer/id #uuid "af0e1058-b843-5261-b5a1-91f185eb6d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286384} {:answer/id #uuid "cf53b765-2868-582d-9cd7-9346da72